DroidWorks U.S.A. – State Distance Module

Lesson Set 01 | 01_State_Distance
Bill of Materials

Working sensorfusion_distance node
Ubuntu (Linux)
ROS 2 Jazzy
Existing droidworks_sensors package

Purpose
This module watches the fused distance over time and extracts higher-level distance state information:

Current trend: Increasing / Decreasing / Stable
Combined situational state (optional)

It turns raw ranging data into something a behavior or OLED display can act on more intelligently.
Create the Node

Place the node file 05_State_Distance into the package
Add the entry point in setup.py:
'state_distance = droidworks_sensors.state_distance:main',

BSR (Build / Source / Run)
 cd ~/droidworks_ws
 colcon build --packages-select droidworks_sensors
 source install/setup.bash
 ros2 run droidworks_sensors state_distance

Verify Results
 ros2 topic echo /distance_trend
 ros2 topic echo /distance_state

Expected behavior
 Move an object slowly toward the sensors → Decreasing
 Move it away → Increasing
 Hold it still → Stable
 The combined state should reflect both the trend and the current personal-space zone

Success = clean, responsive publications that correctly describe whether the object is approaching, receding, or stationary.
